---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: The Abstract
lang: en
description: "The Abstract — Reading the Content Economy from Europe. A newsletter by Claudio Cammarano."
---

<div class="newsletter-content">
    <h1>The Abstract</h1>
    <p class="abstract-tagline">Reading the Content Economy from Europe</p>

    {# Il form sta in cima: questa pagina e' l'atterraggio della pill in nav e
       del blocco nel footer, quindi chi arriva trova subito l'iscrizione e
       poi l'elenco delle uscite.
       L'embed Substack e' un iframe di terza parte con i suoi cookie: viene
       montato solo dopo il consenso. Il link diretto sotto funziona sempre,
       consenso o no, e resta la via di fuga se l'embed non carica. #}
    <div class="newsletter-signup">
        <div class="substack-embed-slot" data-substack-src="https://claudiocammarano.substack.com/embed" data-consent-notice="The subscription form is hosted by Substack and sets its own cookies. It loads once you accept measurement and third-party embeds — or you can subscribe directly on Substack.">
            <p class="substack-embed-fallback">The subscription form is hosted by Substack and sets its own cookies. Use the direct link below, or accept embeds to load it here.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="newsletter-direct">
            <a href="https://claudiocammarano.substack.com/subscribe" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Subscribe on Substack ↗</a>
        </p>
    </div>

    <p>The Abstract is the English-language counterpart of this site. It is a newsletter about what happens to publishing, media, and cultural production in the age of generative AI and fragmenting platforms — written from a European perspective, for readers who share the questions but not the language.</p>

    <p>It began here in 2017 as an Italian blog and was relaunched in 2026 as a long-form newsletter on Substack. New essays appear once or twice a month. The Italian work — on education, publishing, semiotics, and the Italian intellectual tradition — continues on this site; The Abstract is where the same questions travel in English.</p>

    <div class="abstract-ctas">
        <a href="https://claudiocammarano.substack.com/p/the-abstract-eight-years-later" class="btn-about">Read the latest issue →</a>
    </div>

    {% if abstract.posts and abstract.posts.length > 0 %}
    <h2>Recent essays</h2>
    {% for post in abstract.posts %}
    <article class="abstract-essay-card">
      <div class="article-meta">
        {% if post.date %}<span class="article-date">{{ post.date }}</span>{% endif %}
        <span class="article-tag">The Abstract</span>
      </div>
      <h3 class="abstract-essay-card-title">
        <a href="{{ post.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ post.title }} ↗</a>
      </h3>
      {% if loop.index0 == 0 and post.excerpt %}
      <p class="abstract-block-post-excerpt">{{ post.excerpt }}</p>
      {% elif loop.index0 > 0 and post.subtitle %}
      <p class="abstract-block-post-excerpt">{{ post.subtitle }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
</div>

<script>
(function() {
  var slot = document.querySelector('.substack-embed-slot');
  if (!slot) return;
  function mount() {
    if (slot.querySelector('iframe')) return;
    var f = document.createElement('iframe');
    f.className = 'substack-embed substack-embed--page';
    f.src = slot.getAttribute('data-substack-src');
    f.title = 'Subscribe to The Abstract';
    f.width = '480';
    f.height = '320';
    f.loading = 'lazy';
    f.frameBorder = '0';
    f.scrolling = 'no';
    slot.innerHTML = '';
    slot.appendChild(f);
  }
  if (window.ccConsentState === 'granted') mount();
  document.addEventListener('cc:consent', function(e) {
    if (e.detail === 'granted') mount();
  });
})();
</script>
